      "body": "**TLDR:** `Indexer._rotate_activation` multiplies by a 128x128 Hadamard matrix that `functools.cache` kept. A fake-tensor trace filled the cache with a FakeTensor, and every later eager call broke. The matrix is now built on every call; speed is unchanged.\n\n**Problem**\n1. **Cached matrix.** `compressor._hadamard` builds the 128x128 matrix under `functools.cache`, keyed by size, dtype and device.\n2. **Fake first.** A fake-tensor trace (make_fx, GraphTrainer) calls it first and caches a FakeTensor.\n3. **Breaks eager.** Later eager Indexer calls get that FakeTensor back and fail.\n4. **Real first.** In the other order, the trace bakes the cached real tensor in as a constant.\n5. **When.** Nothing on main fake-traces DeepSeek-V4 today, so no run hits it yet.\n\n**Solution**\n1. Drop the cache: `_hadamard` builds the matrix on every call (7 doublings of a small tensor).\n2. Unchanged: the matrix and the Indexer math.\n\n**Results**\nNumerics: identical (the same +1/-1 matrix, built each call instead of read from the cache).\n```text\nDeepSeek-V4 Flash layers 4+5, fwd+bwd wall, 1x GB300, FA4, median of fresh processes\n16k   74.93 -> 75.07 ms  (+0.2%, noise)\n4k    32.00 -> 32.22 ms\n```\nMeasured on top of the DeepSeek-V4 compile stack; this commit changes no compiled region.\n\nNOTE: not measured under CUDA graphs; GraphTrainer end to end not run.\n\n**Test plan**\n`pytest tests/unit_tests/cpu/models/deepseek_v4/test_deepseek_v4_compressor.py -k test_rotate_activation_after_fake_tensor_trace` (fails on main, passes here).\n",
